  "scope": "Seven catalog obligations have conservative empty-subject proofs only. An entirely absent UHVI region cannot be straddled by any selected geometry. Deep-well enclosure requires the deep-well target itself absent, including explicit mask data. Precision-resistor and RPM-selected subjects require empty RPM, URPM, CRPM and poly-resistor purposes. The nwell-hole angle subject requires no holes in the merged nwell and no explicit nwell mask or extended-drain markers. Candidate cell names or labels prevent the associated proof. Nonempty subjects stay unreviewed; source N/A values are not used as waivers. Nonempty rule meanings and complete device qualification remain separate, including the catalog/manual depmos.8 and urpm.3 naming differences.",
